  "welcomeBonus": "500.000 MAP Club points after Rp 5.000.000 spent within 3 months of approval. New primary cards only.",
  "notes": [
    "Sports merchants follow the MCCs in Maybank’s bonus terms, which include clothing stores (5691) and shoe stores (5661).",
    "Fast food (MCC 5814) is on the restaurant bonus list but earns nothing from 10 September 2026.",
    "10x TREATS on Manchester United Premier League win days is not estimated.",
    "TREATS Points are credited as purchases post, with category extras credited separately, so the app checks this card per purchase.",
    "From 10 September 2026 no TREATS on Maybank XBill, XCash, balance conversion, QR payments, taxes and government services (MCC 9211, 9222, 9311, 9399), fast food (MCC 5814), or utility payments (MCC 4900) above Rp 10.000.000. The terms set that limit per card; estimates apply it per purchase. The exclusion list before that date was not retrieved.",
    "Transfers move one for one — 20.000 TREATS for 20.000 KrisFlyer, GarudaMiles or Asia Miles, and 5.000 for 5.000 AirAsia points — until 200.000 miles have been taken in that programme in the twelve months to the transfer. The ceiling is per airline and is not pooled, so KrisFlyer, GarudaMiles and Asia Miles each carry their own and a heavy year can move 600.000 miles across the three. Past a programme’s ceiling the rest converts at 3 TREATS to 1 mile. Each mileage conversion costs Rp 20.000, which estimates do not subtract.",
    "TREATS Points expire one year after they are earned.",
    "A transfer estimate now applies the ceiling. It is spent in whole transfer steps, so a step straddling the ceiling waits for the next window rather than being split, which the issuer's own screens may not do.",
    "The ceiling and the 3:1 beyond it are the terms Maybank set on 1 January 2026. AirAsia points are written the same way; the published change named KrisFlyer, GarudaMiles and Asia Miles, so AirAsia is an assumption."
  ],
